L000279	
L000280	We now turn to the extraction of the $S$-wave $2n$--$2n$ phase shifts from our finite-volume spectra.
L000281	For the realistic N$^{3}$LO chiral EFT Hamiltonian of Ref.~\cite{Elhatisari:2022zrb}, the infinite-volume
L000282	two-neutron system is not bound, but it corresponds to a virtual state.
L000283	Nevertheless, in the periodic boxes used here the lowest $nn$ $S$-wave level is shifted below the
L000284	two-neutron threshold and can be treated as a shallow finite-volume dimer (a quasibound dineutron).
L000285	This provides a practical intermediate description in which the four-neutron finite-volume levels are interpreted
L000286	as two composite dimers in relative motion, and L\"uscher's relation can be used to map the discrete energies
L000287	to elastic $2n$--$2n$ phase shifts.
L000288	
L000289	
L000290	For each box size $L$ we compute the four-neutron energy $E_{4n}^{(L)}$ and the two-neutron energy $E_{2n}^{(L)}$ in the same periodic volume.
L000291	The latter defines the effective finite-volume ``binding'' of the quasibound $2n$ level,
L000292	$B_{2n}^{(L)}\equiv -E_{2n}^{(L)}$.
L000293	To extract the relative momentum $p$ of the two-dineutron system we invert the finite-volume
L000294	dispersion relation for composite dineutrons [Eq.~(\ref{eqn:E-momentum-01})].
L000295	This inversion requires as input the infinite-volume dineutron binding energy $B_{2n}$.
L000296	For the N$^{3}$LO interaction this scale tends to zero as $L\!\to\!\infty$ and cannot be determined directly
L000297	from our largest volumes.
L000298	We therefore treat $B_{2n}$ as an auxiliary near-threshold parameter and scan representative values
L000299	$B_{2n}=0.01$--$0.09$~MeV (all below the smallest $B_{2n}^{(L)}$ encountered at our largest $L$),
L000300	using the resulting spread as an estimate of the residual systematic uncertainty associated with employing
L000301	the finite-volume dineutron picture when the underlying $nn$ pole is virtual.
L000302	
L000303	\begin{figure}[!htbp]
L000304	  \includegraphics[width=0.43\textwidth]{2n-2n-phaseshift-n3lo.pdf}
L000305	  \caption{Dineutron--dineutron $S$-wave scattering phase shift $\delta$ as a function of relative momentum $p$ extracted from finite-volume $4n$ and $2n$ energies using L\"uscher's method and the composite-dimer finite-volume relation in Eq.~(\ref{eqn:E-momentum-01}), for the N$^{3}$LO chiral EFT interaction of Ref.~\cite{Elhatisari:2022zrb}. Different symbols correspond to the scanned near-threshold values of $B_{2n}$ (in MeV), and the shaded band indicates the momentum range associated with $L\simeq 20$--$15$~fm.}
L000306	  \label{fig:phase}
L000307	\end{figure}
L000308	The resulting $2n$--$2n$ $S$-wave phase shifts are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:phase}. At the smallest extracted relative momenta (largest boxes), the phase shifts show the largest sensitivity
L000309	to the auxiliary near-threshold input $B_{2n}$ used in the inversion of Eq.~(\ref{eqn:E-momentum-01}).
L000310	While some of the $B_{2n}$ values yield slightly negative $\delta(p)$ in this regime, the low-momentum trend
L000311	systematically bends toward $\delta(p)\to 0$ as $B_{2n}\to 0$, as expected for short-range interactions. We therefore do not draw a firm conclusion from the sign of the lowest-momentum points in Fig.~\ref{fig:phase}. As the momentum increases, $\delta(p)$ rises, becomes positive, and exhibits a shallow maximum
L000312	of order $10^\circ$ around $p\simeq 60$~MeV, before decreasing again and turning negative at the
L000313	highest momenta shown.
L000314	The dependence on the scanned $B_{2n}$ values is mild over most of the range and is most pronounced
L000315	only at the smallest momenta, where the dineutron size is largest and finite-volume effects are maximally amplified.
L000316	
L000317	In the intermediate window $p\simeq 55$--$100$~MeV, $\delta(p)$ displays a clear nonmonotonic structure,
L000318	indicating a weak attractive feature.
L000319	However, we do not observe the characteristic rapid rise through $90^\circ$ that would signal a narrow
L000320	elastic resonance.
L000321	The shaded band in Fig.~\ref{fig:phase} highlights $p\simeq 60$--$84$~MeV, which corresponds to
L000322	$L\simeq 20$--$15$~fm and (for the same volumes) to confined $4n$ energies in the range
L000323	$E_{4n}\simeq 1.7$--$3.3$~MeV (cf.~Fig.~1), overlapping the experimentally reported correlated $4n$ peak
L000324	at $2.37\pm0.38\text{(stat.)}\pm0.44\text{(sys.)}$~MeV.
L000325	
L000326	
L000327	Our results are qualitatively consistent with previous investigations of $2n$--$2n$ scattering phase shifts using rigorous solutions of FY and AGS equations~\cite{Deltuva:2019mnv}, which found that at physical interaction strengths, a bound tetraneutron state evolves into a virtual state rather than a resonance. While we identify a weak nonmonotonic attraction at intermediate momenta in the current framework, the phase shift remains well below $90^\circ$, supporting the conclusion that no observable narrow resonance exists at the physical point.
L000328	
L000329	
L000330	\section{Summary}
L000331	
L000332	We have investigated the tetraneutron system confined in a cubic box using nuclear lattice effective field theory, with box sizes up to $L = 30$~fm.
L000333	Using the N$^{3}$LO chiral EFT interaction, the confined $4n$ energy decreases gradually with increasing $L$ and remains concave over the explored volumes, showing no plateau that would be characteristic of a narrow resonance.
L000334	For comparison, we also repeat the confined-spectrum calculation with an SU(4)-symmetric interaction fitted to the $^1$S$_0$ phase shifts; the SU(4) results are consistent with the N$^{3}$LO trend and are reported in~\cite{SM}.
L000335	
L000336	
L000337	
L000338	To interpret possible $4n$ correlations in terms of two-dineutron dynamics, we employ the finite-volume dineutron approximation, where the lowest $nn$ $S$-wave level in a periodic box is quasibound even though the infinite-volume $nn$ system corresponds to a virtual state.
L000339	Within this framework, we validate the L\"uscher-based extraction by studying $n$--$n$ and $n$--$2n$ scattering.
L000340	The ratio of scattering lengths $a_{n-2n}/a_{n-n}$ exhibits the expected universal behavior for near-threshold systems, with deviations only when $B_{2n}\approx 0.01$~MeV, where the proximity to the virtual-state regime amplifies finite-volume and lattice-spacing effects.
L000341	
L000342	
L000343	We then extract the $2n$--$2n$ $S$-wave phase shifts from finite-volume $4n$ and $2n$ energies using L\"uscher's method together with the composite-dineutron finite-volume relation.
L000344	
L000345	At the smallest momenta, the extracted phase shifts show the largest
L000346	sensitivity to $B_{2n}$. While for some of $B_{2n}$ values we observe slightly negative
L000347	$\delta(p)$ in this regime, the low-momentum trend bends toward $\delta(p)\to 0$ as
L000348	$B_{2n}\to 0$, and we therefore do not draw a firm conclusion from the
L000349	sign of the lowest-momentum points.
L000350	In the intermediate window $p\simeq 55$--$100$~MeV, $\delta(p)$ becomes positive and shows a shallow nonmonotonic structure, with a maximum of order $10^\circ$ around $p\simeq 60$--$84$~MeV, but without a rapid rise through $90^\circ$ typical of a narrow elastic resonance.
L000351	This momentum band corresponds to box sizes $L\simeq 20$--$15$~fm and confined $4n$ energies of $1.7$--$3.3$~MeV, which lie close to the experimentally reported correlated $4n$ peak at $2.37\pm0.38\text{(stat.)}\pm0.44\text{(sys.)}$~MeV.
L000352	
L000353	In the future, we plan to extend the NLEFT framework~\cite{Elhatisari:2015iga} to investigate the $^8$He($p,p^4$He)$4n$ reaction and understand the correlated structures observed. As a first step in this direction, NLEFT has recently been used to quantify four-neutron correlation patterns in $^{7}$H and $^{8}$He, motivated by quasifree knockout measurements~\cite{Zhang:2025uin}.
